SPF + DKIM → result
↓
DMARC p= → action

SPF and DKIM give pass/fail results.
DMARC decides what to do with those results.

p= defines action for main domain
sp= defines action for subdomains

If sp=none → subdomains are not strictly protected
but vulnerability only exists if spoofed email reaches inbox

  p = main domain rule
sp = subdomain rule
DMARC = decision maker



  SPF  → Sender Policy Framework
DKIM → DomainKeys Identified Mail
DMARC → Domain-based Message Authentication, Reporting & Conformance

p   → Policy (main domain)
sp  → Subdomain Policy
rua → Aggregate report email
ruf → Forensic report email


adkim → DKIM alignment mode
aspf  → SPF alignment mode
